questions.explanation:
Hint:\(p=\dfrac{1}{3}\rho v_{rms}^2\)

Step 1: The pressure exerted by ideal gas of the walls of the container is given
by;
\(p=\dfrac{1}{3}\rho v_{vrms}^2~~~...(1) \)
The rms speed of the ideal gas is given by;
\(v_{rms}=\sqrt{\dfrac{3RT}{M}} ~~~...(2) \)
By using above two equations;
\(\Rightarrow p=\dfrac{\rho RT}{M}\)
Step 2:Find the average force exerted by the ideal gas;
\(\dfrac{F_{avg}}{A}=\dfrac{\rho RT}{M}\)
Therefore;
\(\Rightarrow F_{avg}=\dfrac{\rho ART}{M} \)
From the above expression the average force by the ideal gas on the walls of a
closed container depends on\(T^1 \).
